# crown-pages-types — Workflow

## Package Distribution

This is a **private package distributed via GitHub**, NOT published to npm.

- Package name: `@crown-pages/types`
- Installed as: `"github:phn-team/crown-pages-types"` in both consumer repos
- Version is managed manually in `package.json` (`1.0.0`)
- Schema version constant: `SCHEMA_VERSION = '1.0.0'` in `src/sections/index.ts`

## Making Changes — Full Chain

Every change to this package requires updating BOTH consumer repos and redeploying:

```
1. Edit src/ files
2. npm run build          ← compiles TypeScript to dist/
3. git commit + push      ← makes it available via GitHub install
4. In pages-mobile:  npm run update:types
5. In pages:         npm run update:types
6. Redeploy pages (Vercel) + submit EAS build for pages-mobile
```

**Do not skip steps.** If you push types but forget to run `update:types` in a consumer repo, that repo will be running stale types.

## Local Dev Shortcut (pages-mobile only)

`npm run sync:types` in `pages-mobile` copies directly from `D:/GitHub/crown-pages-types` into `node_modules/@crown-pages/types`. Use this during active development to test changes instantly without committing. Does NOT update from GitHub.

## Section Definition Structure

Each section in `src/sections/index.ts` follows this shape:

```ts
{
  type: string,           // unique identifier, e.g. 'hero'
  name: string,           // display name
  description: string,
  category: 'content' | 'media' | 'interaction' | 'data' | 'layout',
  icon: { mobile: string, web: string },  // Ionicons / Lucide icon names
  fields: FieldDefinition[],  // TextField, ImageField, ArrayField, etc.
  defaultData: Record<string, unknown>,
  styleOptions: { canOverride: string[], colorFields: string[], defaultStyles: {} },
  renderingHints: { mobile: {}, web: {} },
  version: '1.0.0'
}
```

## Current Section Types (16 defined)

`hero`, `features`, `about`, `contact`, `personalContact`, `gallery`, `testimonials`, `faq`, `cta`, `multiContact`, `medicalProvider`, `companyHeader`, `contactCard`, `amenities`, `linksWithContact`, `socialLinks`

`linksWithContact` — now fully defined in types with all contact fields (`contactName`, `contactRole`, `contactPhone`, `contactPhone2`, `contactEmail`, `contactFax`, `contactWebsite`, `contactImageUrl`) and `mediaItems` per link (vertical photo/video stacking). The old mobile editor split-hack has been removed.

**Note:** `companyHeader`, `contactCard`, and `amenities` are also in `LOCAL_SECTION_DEFINITIONS` in `pages-mobile/app/(app)/page-editor/[id].tsx`. `linksWithContact` is now only in this package (the mobile local shims were removed). Keep both in sync when editing the other three.

## Adding a New Section Type

1. Add definition to `src/sections/index.ts`
2. Add to `SECTION_DEFINITIONS` array
3. `npm run build`
4. `git commit + push`
5. `npm run update:types` in `pages-mobile` → add editor component
6. `npm run update:types` in `pages` → add renderer component + register in `getSectionComponent()` in `enhanced-page-renderer.tsx`
7. Redeploy both apps
